# Build-context filter for apps/web/Dockerfile ONLY (BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile; the context is the repo
# root). Keeps host artefacts out of the build: the host's node_modules (the
# image installs its own, and it is ~90 MB to upload), a developer's .env
# files (which would bake a localhost API URL into the bundle), and build
# output. The image needs package.json, package-lock.json, packages/shared and
# apps/web/{package.json,index.html,vite.config.js,public,src,nginx.conf}.

**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/dist
apps/api
apps/web/test
docs
scripts
